            "review_title": "Review at Chaykhana",
            "review_text": "Иван С\n3 contributions\n0\nI DO NOT recommend\nMar 2024 • Friends\nWe received a beautiful advertising flyer on the beach and were seduced by a beautiful picture.\nIn summary: there is no interior, everything is old and dirty, the smelly toilet is shared with the massage parlor (one cubicle!).\nThe restaurant is empty.\nFood: we arrived at 20:50, the grill was no longer working, and it was Friday, March 8th for a minute... They couldn’t cook anything other than what was already ready.\nHeated pilaf with very dry meat, manti with veins, lagman and shurpa are very tasty.\nWine is the icing on the cake. Before taking a bottle of red wine, I asked for a glass, they brought a cloudy and sour liquid from the refrigerator... I asked what it was, apparently the hostess came and started shouting that this was an excellent California wine of 2014, they all tried it and were delighted. I didn’t drink it, but they categorically refused to remove it from the check.\nWe ordered freshly squeezed juice, at first they forgot it, they brought it at the end of dinner, we asked to pour it into a container to take with us, but alas, there were no takeaway glasses either.\nI DO NOT RECOMMEND\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nShow original\nWritten March 8, 2024",
